       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical upper-range dose\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and add the clinical rationale. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
