       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is double the maximum labeled daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and more ibuprofen won't add analgesic benefit. I'm not comfortable placing it, even with your confirmation.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the absolute maximum, with a note about short-term use and GI protection)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically necessary, please discuss it with the pharmacist or the attending and place the order through the hospital's dose-override process. If a 1,600 mg total daily dose was the intent, tell me and I'll enter it."
